  <h2>Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    This policy guides the creation and publication of content on the SPMH
    Newsroom (<a href='https://newsroom.spmh.co.ke'>newsroom.spmh.co.ke</a>). It
    ensures that everything we publish is accurate, dignified, aligned with our
    mission, and respectful of the privacy of our patients and staff.
  </p>

  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>The Newsroom hosts four types of content:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Stories (articles)</strong> — in-depth reporting and features on hospital
      activity, milestones, clinical programmes, and community impact.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Blog</strong> — lighter, more frequent posts written by staff, students,
      and partners in a personal voice.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Press Releases</strong> — formal, dated statements issued for external
      distribution to media, partners, and regulators.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Events</strong> — announcements of medical camps, community outreaches,
      CPD sessions, and stakeholder forums.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
  <p>
    The Newsroom reports on the hospital's work in a way that is honest,
    accurate, and consistent with our mission. Stories are not published or
    withheld for the purpose of commercial gain or personal interest. Where
    reporting covers sensitive topics — such as patient outcomes, complaints, or
    institutional challenges — the editorial team retains the independence to
    report accurately, while respecting patient dignity and confidentiality.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and sourcing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      All factual claims must be verifiable from a primary source (hospital
      records, interviews, official documents).
    </li>
    <li>
      Quotations must be accurate and approved by the person quoted before
      publication.
    </li>
    <li>Statistics must cite their source and date.</li>
    <li>
      Where information is uncertain or contested, this must be stated clearly
      in the article.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Patient privacy and consent</h2>
  <p>
    Patient confidentiality is protected by law and by Catholic ethical
    standards. The following rules apply to any story involving a patient:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Written, informed consent must be obtained from the patient (or guardian,
      for minors) before publishing their name, image, or identifiable details.
    </li>
    <li>
      Consent must include a clear description of where and how the story will
      be published.
    </li>
    <li>
      Patients may withdraw consent at any time before publication, and may
      request removal after publication where feasible.
    </li>
    <li>
      In stories about sensitive health conditions — HIV, mental illness,
      gender-based violence, maternal complications — additional care must be
      taken to protect identity, even where a patient consents.
    </li>
    <li>
      Photographs of clinical areas must not identify patients who have not
      consented.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    We correct errors promptly, transparently, and visibly. When a story has
    been published with a factual error:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The correction is added to the bottom of the article, with the date.
    </li>
    <li>
      For significant errors, the headline or lead may be revised and a note
      added explaining the change.
    </li>
    <li>
      Corrections are logged and reviewed quarterly to identify systemic issues.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Corrections may be submitted to <a href='mailto:editorial@spmh.co.ke'
      >editorial@spmh.co.ke</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Contributions</h2>
  <p>
    We welcome contributions from hospital staff, students, partners, and
    community members. Contributions are accepted on the following basis:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      All contributions are reviewed by the editorial team before publication.
    </li>
    <li>
      The editorial team may edit for clarity, length, tone, and alignment with
      the policy.
    </li>
    <li>
      Contributors are credited by name, unless they request anonymity and the
      editorial team agrees.
    </li>
    <li>
      Contribution does not confer ownership of the published piece — copyright
      remains with SPMH.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Approval authority</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Content type</th>
        <th>Approver</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td>Stories and Blog posts</td><td
          >Communications Officer or Hospital Administrator</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td>Press Releases</td><td
          >Hospital Administrator, in consultation with the Board where required</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr><td>Event listings</td><td>Communications Officer</td></tr>
      <tr
        ><td
          >Sensitive topics (patient outcomes, complaints, institutional
          challenges)</td
        ><td
          >Hospital Administrator, and where required the Catholic Diocese of
          Homa Bay</td
        ></tr
      >
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Review</h2>
  <p>
    This policy is reviewed every two years by the Hospital Management Team and
    approved by the Board of Management.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
